<?xml version="1.0" ?>
<usx version="3.0">
  <book code="1PE" style="id">1 PETER</book>
  <chapter number="1" style="c" sid="1PE 1"/>
  <para style="s1">Greeting</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="1" style="v" sid="1PE 1:1"/>
    Peter, entrusted by Jesus Christ with apostolic authority, 
    <verse eid="1PE 1:1"/>
  </para>
  <para style="p">To the chosen ones who live as exiles scattered throughout Pontus, Galatia, Cappadocia, Asia, and Bithynia,</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="2" style="v" sid="1PE 1:2"/>
    chosen according to the foreknowledge of God the Father, through the sanctifying work of the Spirit, resulting in obedience and the sprinkling of the blood of Jesus Christ:
    <verse eid="1PE 1:2"/>
  </para>
  <para style="p">May grace and peace be multiplied to you.</para>
  <para style="s1">Ascription of Blessing to God</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="3" style="v" sid="1PE 1:3"/>
    Praised be the God and Father of our Lord Jesus Christ, who in His abundant mercy has given us new birth into a living hope through the resurrection of Jesus Christ from the dead,
    <verse eid="1PE 1:3"/>
  </para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="4" style="v" sid="1PE 1:4"/>
    into an inheritance that is imperishable, uncontaminated, and unfading, kept safe in heaven for you,
    <verse eid="1PE 1:4"/>
  </para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="5" style="v" sid="1PE 1:5"/>
    who are being protected by God’s power through faith for a salvation prepared to be disclosed in the final age.
    <verse eid="1PE 1:5"/>
  </para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="6" style="v" sid="1PE 1:6"/>
    In this reality you rejoice greatly, even though presently for a brief period, if it must be so, you have been distressed by various trials,
    <verse eid="1PE 1:6"/>
  </para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="7" style="v" sid="1PE 1:7"/>
    in order that the proven genuineness of your faith—far more precious than gold that perishes despite being refined by fire—may result in praise, glory, and honor when Jesus Christ is revealed.
    <verse eid="1PE 1:7"/>
  </para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="8" style="v" sid="1PE 1:8"/>
    Though you have not seen Him, you love Him; and though you do not see Him now, you believe in Him and greatly rejoice with inexpressible and glorious joy,
    <verse eid="1PE 1:8"/>
  </para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="9" style="v" sid="1PE 1:9"/>
    as you receive the outcome of your faith—the salvation of your souls.
    <verse eid="1PE 1:9"/>
  </para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="10" style="v" sid="1PE 1:10"/>
    Regarding this salvation, the prophets who prophesied about the grace promised to you searched diligently and investigated carefully,
    <verse eid="1PE 1:10"/>
  </para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="11" style="v" sid="1PE 1:11"/>
    seeking to discover what person or what time the Spirit of Christ within them was pointing to when He testified in advance about the sufferings prepared for Christ and the glories that would follow them.
    <verse eid="1PE 1:11"/>
  </para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="12" style="v" sid="1PE 1:12"/>
    It was disclosed to them that they were serving not their own interests but yours, concerning the very matters that have now been proclaimed to you through those who announced the good news to you by the Holy Spirit sent from heaven—matters that angels desire to examine closely.
    <verse eid="1PE 1:12"/>
  </para>
  <para style="s1">Called to Be Holy</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="13" style="v" sid="1PE 1:13"/>
    Therefore, preparing your minds for action and exercising self-discipline, set your hope fully on the grace that will be brought to you at the revelation of Jesus Christ.
    <verse eid="1PE 1:13"/>
  </para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="14" style="v" sid="1PE 1:14"/>
    As children characterized by obedience, do not allow yourselves to be shaped by the desires that formerly controlled you in your ignorance.
    <verse eid="1PE 1:14"/>
  </para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="15" style="v" sid="1PE 1:15"/>
    Rather, just as the One who summoned you is holy, so you yourselves must become holy in your entire way of life,
    <verse eid="1PE 1:15"/>
  </para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="16" style="v" sid="1PE 1:16"/>
    because it stands written: “You shall be holy, for I am holy.”*
    <verse eid="1PE 1:16"/>
  </para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="17" style="v" sid="1PE 1:17"/>
    And since you address as Father the One who judges each person impartially based on that person's deeds, conduct yourselves with reverent fear throughout the period of your temporary residence on earth,
    <verse eid="1PE 1:17"/>
  </para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="18" style="v" sid="1PE 1:18"/>
    recognizing that you were ransomed from the empty way of life handed down from your ancestors, not with perishable commodities such as silver or gold,
    <verse eid="1PE 1:18"/>
  </para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="19" style="v" sid="1PE 1:19"/>
    but with the precious blood of Christ, like that of a lamb without defect or blemish.
    <verse eid="1PE 1:19"/>
  </para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="20" style="v" sid="1PE 1:20"/>
    He was foreknown before the world’s foundation but was manifested in these final times for your sake—
    <verse eid="1PE 1:20"/>
  </para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="21" style="v" sid="1PE 1:21"/>
    you who through Him trust in God, who raised Him from the dead and granted Him glory, so that your faith and hope rest in God.
    <verse eid="1PE 1:21"/>
  </para>
  <para style="s1">The Abiding Word</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="22" style="v" sid="1PE 1:22"/>
    Having purified your souls through obedience to the truth for genuine brotherly affection, love one another deeply from a pure heart,
    <verse eid="1PE 1:22"/>
  </para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="23" style="v" sid="1PE 1:23"/>
    for you have been born anew, not from perishable seed but from imperishable seed, through the living and enduring word of God.
    <verse eid="1PE 1:23"/>
  </para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="24" style="v" sid="1PE 1:24"/>
    For “all flesh is like grass,
    <verse eid="1PE 1:24"/>
  </para>
  <para style="p">and all its glory like the flower of grass.</para>
  <para style="p">The grass withers</para>
  <para style="p">and the flower drops off,</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="25" style="v" sid="1PE 1:25"/>
    but the Lord’s word endures forever.”*
    <verse eid="1PE 1:25"/>
  </para>
  <para style="p">This is the word that was proclaimed to you as good news.</para>
  <para style="s1">Notes</para>
  <para style="p">16 Quoted from Lev. 11:44</para>
  <para style="p">25 Quoted from Is. 40:6, 8</para>
  <chapter eid="1PE 1"/>
  <chapter number="2" style="c" sid="1PE 2"/>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="1" style="v" sid="1PE 2:1"/>
    Therefore, strip away all malice, all deceit, hypocrisy, envy, and all slanderous speech.
    <verse eid="1PE 2:1"/>
  </para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="2" style="v" sid="1PE 2:2"/>
    Like newborn babies, crave the pure spiritual milk, so that through it you may grow up into the fullness of salvation—
    <verse eid="1PE 2:2"/>
  </para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="3" style="v" sid="1PE 2:3"/>
    if indeed you have tasted that the Lord is good.
    <verse eid="1PE 2:3"/>
  </para>
  <para style="s1">The Living Stone and His Chosen People</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="4" style="v" sid="1PE 2:4"/>
    As you approach Him—a living stone rejected by human beings but chosen and valuable in God’s eyes—
    <verse eid="1PE 2:4"/>
  </para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="5" style="v" sid="1PE 2:5"/>
    you yourselves, like living stones, are being constructed into a spiritual house to serve as a holy priesthood, presenting spiritual sacrifices acceptable to God through Jesus Christ.
    <verse eid="1PE 2:5"/>
  </para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="6" style="v" sid="1PE 2:6"/>
    For Scripture contains this statement:
    <verse eid="1PE 2:6"/>
  </para>
  <para style="p">“Look, I am laying in Zion a stone,</para>
  <para style="p">a chosen and precious cornerstone,</para>
  <para style="p">and whoever believes in Him will never be disappointed.”*</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="7" style="v" sid="1PE 2:7"/>
    To you who believe, therefore, belongs the honor, 
    <verse eid="1PE 2:7"/>
  </para>
  <para style="p">but to those who refuse to believe,</para>
  <para style="p">“The stone that the builders rejected—</para>
  <para style="p">this very one has become the cornerstone,”*</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="8" style="v" sid="1PE 2:8"/>
    and “A stone that causes stumbling 
    <verse eid="1PE 2:8"/>
  </para>
  <para style="p">and a rock that brings offense.”*</para>
  <para style="p">They stumble because they disobey the message—which is also what they were appointed to do.</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="9" style="v" sid="1PE 2:9"/>
    But you are a chosen race, a royal priesthood, a holy nation, a people belonging exclusively to God, so that you may declare the praises of the One who summoned you out of darkness into His amazing light.
    <verse eid="1PE 2:9"/>
  </para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="10" style="v" sid="1PE 2:10"/>
    Once you were not a people, but now you are God’s people; once you had not received mercy, but now you have received mercy.
    <verse eid="1PE 2:10"/>
  </para>
  <para style="s1">Christians’ Honorable Conduct and Just Suffering</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="11" style="v" sid="1PE 2:11"/>
    Beloved, I appeal to you: Recognize yourselves as temporary residents and exiles in this world, and therefore resist the bodily appetites that battle against your soul.
    <verse eid="1PE 2:11"/>
  </para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="12" style="v" sid="1PE 2:12"/>
    Let your behavior among unbelievers be exemplary, so that when they slander you as evildoers, your manifest goodness will lead them to praise God when He arrives in judgment.
    <verse eid="1PE 2:12"/>
  </para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="13" style="v" sid="1PE 2:13"/>
    Accept the authority of human governing institutions out of loyalty to the Lord—whether the emperor or highest ruler,
    <verse eid="1PE 2:13"/>
  </para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="14" style="v" sid="1PE 2:14"/>
    or regional administrators whom he delegates to prosecute criminals and honor the law-abiding.
    <verse eid="1PE 2:14"/>
  </para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="15" style="v" sid="1PE 2:15"/>
    The intention of God is that your upright lives should silence the slander of those who speak against you in their ignorance.
    <verse eid="1PE 2:15"/>
  </para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="16" style="v" sid="1PE 2:16"/>
    Conduct yourselves as liberated people, yet never exploit that liberty as license for wickedness; rather, live as those bound in service to God.
    <verse eid="1PE 2:16"/>
  </para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="17" style="v" sid="1PE 2:17"/>
    Treat all people with dignity. Love your fellow believers. Revere God. Respect the ruling authority.
    <verse eid="1PE 2:17"/>
  </para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="18" style="v" sid="1PE 2:18"/>
    Those in household service: Accept the authority of your masters with profound deference—not merely when they treat you fairly and gently, but even when they are severe.
    <verse eid="1PE 2:18"/>
  </para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="19" style="v" sid="1PE 2:19"/>
    It is praiseworthy when someone bears suffering unjustly because their conscience is oriented toward God.
    <verse eid="1PE 2:19"/>
  </para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="20" style="v" sid="1PE 2:20"/>
    There is no virtue in accepting punishment you deserve for wrongdoing. But enduring hardship despite innocent conduct—this merits the approval of God.
    <verse eid="1PE 2:20"/>
  </para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="21" style="v" sid="1PE 2:21"/>
    This is precisely the vocation to which you were appointed, since Christ suffered on your behalf, providing a pattern for you to trace with your own lives—
    <verse eid="1PE 2:21"/>
  </para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="22" style="v" sid="1PE 2:22"/>
    He who was utterly sinless, whose speech contained no falsehood;
    <verse eid="1PE 2:22"/>
  </para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="23" style="v" sid="1PE 2:23"/>
    who, when reviled, returned no abuse; who, when tortured, uttered no threats, but continuously surrendered Himself to the righteous Judge;
    <verse eid="1PE 2:23"/>
  </para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="24" style="v" sid="1PE 2:24"/>
    who bore the weight of our transgressions in His own flesh on the tree, that we might become dead to sin and alive to righteousness; by His wounds your healing was accomplished.
    <verse eid="1PE 2:24"/>
  </para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="25" style="v" sid="1PE 2:25"/>
    You once wandered astray like directionless sheep, but have now come home to the Shepherd and Overseer of your souls. 
    <verse eid="1PE 2:25"/>
  </para>
  <para style="s1">Notes</para>
  <para style="p">6 Quoted from Is. 28:16</para>
  <para style="p">7 Quoted from Ps. 118:22</para>
  <para style="p">8 Quoted from Is. 8:14</para>
  <chapter eid="1PE 2"/>
  <chapter number="3" style="c" sid="1PE 3"/>
  <para style="s1">Submission to Husbands</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="1" style="v" sid="1PE 3:1"/>
    Similarly, wives, submit yourselves to your own husbands, so that even if some refuse to obey the word, they may be won over without words through their wives’ conduct,
    <verse eid="1PE 3:1"/>
  </para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="2" style="v" sid="1PE 3:2"/>
    when they witness your respectful and pure behavior.
    <verse eid="1PE 3:2"/>
  </para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="3" style="v" sid="1PE 3:3"/>
    Your adornment should not be external—braiding hair, wearing gold jewelry, or putting on fine clothes—
    <verse eid="1PE 3:3"/>
  </para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="4" style="v" sid="1PE 3:4"/>
    but rather the inner person of the heart, with the imperishable beauty of a gentle and quiet spirit, which is of great worth in God’s sight.
    <verse eid="1PE 3:4"/>
  </para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="5" style="v" sid="1PE 3:5"/>
    For this is how the holy women of the past who placed their hope in God used to adorn themselves, by submitting to their own husbands,
    <verse eid="1PE 3:5"/>
  </para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="6" style="v" sid="1PE 3:6"/>
    just as Sarah obeyed Abraham, addressing him as master. You have become her daughters when you do what is right without giving way to fear.
    <verse eid="1PE 3:6"/>
  </para>
  <para style="s1">Instruction for Husbands</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="7" style="v" sid="1PE 3:7"/>
    Husbands, likewise, live with your wives in an understanding way, showing honor to the woman as the weaker partner, since you are joint heirs of the gracious gift of life, so that nothing will obstruct your prayers.
    <verse eid="1PE 3:7"/>
  </para>
  <para style="s1">Called to Inherit a Blessing</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="8" style="v" sid="1PE 3:8"/>
    Finally, all of you should be united in spirit, sympathetic, showing brotherly love, compassionate, and humble.
    <verse eid="1PE 3:8"/>
  </para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="9" style="v" sid="1PE 3:9"/>
    Do not repay evil with evil or insult with insult, but on the contrary, offer a blessing, because you were called to this so that you might inherit a blessing.
    <verse eid="1PE 3:9"/>
  </para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="10" style="v" sid="1PE 3:10"/>
    For,
    <verse eid="1PE 3:10"/>
  </para>
  <para style="p">“Whoever desires to love life</para>
  <para style="p">and see good days must restrain his tongue from evil</para>
  <para style="p">and his lips from speaking deception.</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="11" style="v" sid="1PE 3:11"/>
    He must turn away from evil and practice good;
    <verse eid="1PE 3:11"/>
  </para>
  <para style="p">he must pursue peace and chase after it.</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="12" style="v" sid="1PE 3:12"/>
    For the Lord’s eyes rest on the righteous,
    <verse eid="1PE 3:12"/>
  </para>
  <para style="p">and His ears are attentive to their prayer.</para>
  <para style="p">But the Lord’s face is set against those who practice evil.”*</para>
  <para style="s1">Suffering for Righteous Cause</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="13" style="v" sid="1PE 3:13"/>
    Who will harm you if you become enthusiastic about doing good?
    <verse eid="1PE 3:13"/>
  </para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="14" style="v" sid="1PE 3:14"/>
    But even if you should suffer for the sake of righteousness, you are blessed. “Do not fear what they fear or be disturbed.”*
    <verse eid="1PE 3:14"/>
  </para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="15" style="v" sid="1PE 3:15"/>
    Rather, sanctify or set apart Christ as Lord in your hearts, always prepared to give a defense to anyone who asks you to account for the hope you possess—yet do so with gentleness and reverence,
    <verse eid="1PE 3:15"/>
  </para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="16" style="v" sid="1PE 3:16"/>
    maintaining a good conscience, so that those who speak maliciously against your good conduct in Christ may be put to shame regarding the matters in which they slander you.
    <verse eid="1PE 3:16"/>
  </para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="17" style="v" sid="1PE 3:17"/>
    For it is better to suffer for doing good, if that is God’s will, than for doing evil.
    <verse eid="1PE 3:17"/>
  </para>
  <para style="s1">The Example and Purpose of the Suffering of Jesus</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="18" style="v" sid="1PE 3:18"/>
    For Christ also suffered once for sins, the righteous on behalf of the unrighteous, in order to bring you to God. He was put to death in the flesh but made alive in the Spirit,
    <verse eid="1PE 3:18"/>
  </para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="19" style="v" sid="1PE 3:19"/>
    in which He also went and made proclamation to the spirits in prison—
    <verse eid="1PE 3:19"/>
  </para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="20" style="v" sid="1PE 3:20"/>
    those who disobeyed long ago when God waited patiently in Noah’s day, while the ark was being constructed. In the ark a few people, specifically eight souls, were rescued through water.
    <verse eid="1PE 3:20"/>
  </para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="21" style="v" sid="1PE 3:21"/>
    This water symbolizes the baptism that now rescues you—not the removal of physical dirt, but the request to God for a clear conscience—through the resurrection of Jesus Christ,
    <verse eid="1PE 3:21"/>
  </para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="22" style="v" sid="1PE 3:22"/>
    who has gone into heaven and is at the right hand of God, with angels, authorities, and powers subjected to Him.
    <verse eid="1PE 3:22"/>
  </para>
  <para style="s1">Notes</para>
  <para style="p">10-12 Quoted from Ps. 34:12-16</para>
  <para style="p">14 Quoted from Is. 8:12b</para>
  <chapter eid="1PE 3"/>
  <chapter number="4" style="c" sid="1PE 4"/>
  <para style="s1">Living for God’s Will</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="1" style="v" sid="1PE 4:1"/>
    Since Christ suffered in the flesh, arm yourselves with the same mindset, because whoever has suffered in the flesh has finished with sin,
    <verse eid="1PE 4:1"/>
  </para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="2" style="v" sid="1PE 4:2"/>
    in order to live the remainder of your earthly life no longer for human passions but for God’s will.
    <verse eid="1PE 4:2"/>
  </para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="3" style="v" sid="1PE 4:3"/>
    For the time already passed is sufficient for having pursued what the Gentiles desire—living in debauchery, lusts, drunkenness, wild parties, carousing, and detestable idolatry.
    <verse eid="1PE 4:3"/>
  </para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="4" style="v" sid="1PE 4:4"/>
    They find it strange that you do not plunge with them into the same flood of reckless excess, and they heap abuse on you.
    <verse eid="1PE 4:4"/>
  </para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="5" style="v" sid="1PE 4:5"/>
    They will have to give account to the One who stands ready to judge the living and the dead.
    <verse eid="1PE 4:5"/>
  </para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="6" style="v" sid="1PE 4:6"/>
    For this purpose the gospel was proclaimed even to those who are now dead, so that although they were judged in the flesh according to human standards, they might live in the spirit according to God’s standards.
    <verse eid="1PE 4:6"/>
  </para>
  <para style="s1">The End of All Things Has Drawn Near</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="7" style="v" sid="1PE 4:7"/>
    The end of all things is near. Therefore, be of sound judgment and sober-minded for the purpose of prayer.
    <verse eid="1PE 4:7"/>
  </para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="8" style="v" sid="1PE 4:8"/>
    Above everything else, maintain intense love for one another, because love covers a multitude of sins.
    <verse eid="1PE 4:8"/>
  </para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="9" style="v" sid="1PE 4:9"/>
    Show hospitality to one another without complaining.
    <verse eid="1PE 4:9"/>
  </para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="10" style="v" sid="1PE 4:10"/>
    As each one has received a gift, use it to serve one another as faithful stewards of God’s varied grace.
    <verse eid="1PE 4:10"/>
  </para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="11" style="v" sid="1PE 4:11"/>
    If anyone speaks, let him speak as one conveying God’s own words; if anyone serves, let him serve with the strength God provides, so that in all things God may be glorified through Jesus Christ, to whom belong the glory and the power forever and ever. Amen.
    <verse eid="1PE 4:11"/>
  </para>
  <para style="s1">Sharing in the Sufferings of Christ</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="12" style="v" sid="1PE 4:12"/>
    Beloved, do not be surprised at the painful trial you are experiencing, as though something unusual were happening to you.
    <verse eid="1PE 4:12"/>
  </para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="13" style="v" sid="1PE 4:13"/>
    Rather, to the degree that you participate in Christ’s sufferings, rejoice, so that you may also rejoice and be overjoyed when His glory is revealed.
    <verse eid="1PE 4:13"/>
  </para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="14" style="v" sid="1PE 4:14"/>
    When you endure reproach on account of allegiance to Christ, you are blessed, for the Spirit of glory—indeed, the very Spirit of God—rests on you.
    <verse eid="1PE 4:14"/>
  </para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="15" style="v" sid="1PE 4:15"/>
    Ensure that none among you experiences punishment as one guilty of murder, theft, criminal conduct, or intrusion into matters beyond your concern.
    <verse eid="1PE 4:15"/>
  </para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="16" style="v" sid="1PE 4:16"/>
    Yet should someone undergo hardship for bearing the identity of a follower of Christ, let there be no shame in this; rather, let him honor God by carrying that designation.
    <verse eid="1PE 4:16"/>
  </para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="17" style="v" sid="1PE 4:17"/>
    The appointed moment has arrived for divine judgment to commence with the household of God, and if such reckoning starts with us, what end awaits those who defy the gospel of God?
    <verse eid="1PE 4:17"/>
  </para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="18" style="v" sid="1PE 4:18"/>
    And,
    <verse eid="1PE 4:18"/>
  </para>
  <para style="p">“If the righteous person is barely saved,</para>
  <para style="p">where will the ungodly and sinner appear?”*</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="19" style="v" sid="1PE 4:19"/>
    Therefore, let those who suffer according to God’s will entrust their souls to their faithful Creator while continuing to do good.
    <verse eid="1PE 4:19"/>
  </para>
  <para style="s1">Notes</para>
  <para style="p">18 Quoted from Prov. 11:31</para>
  <chapter eid="1PE 4"/>
  <chapter number="5" style="c" sid="1PE 5"/>
  <para style="s1">Shepherding the Flock of God</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="1" style="v" sid="1PE 5:1"/>
    I exhort the elders among you as one who is himself a fellow elder, who bore witness to the sufferings of Christ, and who anticipates participating in the glory soon to be revealed:
    <verse eid="1PE 5:1"/>
  </para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="2" style="v" sid="1PE 5:2"/>
    Shepherd the flock of God placed in your charge, exercising oversight—not from obligation, but from voluntary devotion, in accordance with the will of God; not motivated by sordid profit, but with genuine enthusiasm;
    <verse eid="1PE 5:2"/>
  </para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="3" style="v" sid="1PE 5:3"/>
    not wielding tyrannical control over those entrusted to your guardianship, but modeling exemplary conduct before the flock.
    <verse eid="1PE 5:3"/>
  </para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="4" style="v" sid="1PE 5:4"/>
    When the Supreme Shepherd is manifested, you will obtain the imperishable crown of honor.
    <verse eid="1PE 5:4"/>
  </para>
  <para style="s1">Submission to the Elders</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="5" style="v" sid="1PE 5:5"/>
    In the same way, the younger believers are to place themselves under the authority of the elders. In fact, every one of you must adopt a posture of humility toward others, because,
    <verse eid="1PE 5:5"/>
  </para>
  <para style="p">“God arrays Himself against the arrogant,</para>
  <para style="p">yet extends favor to those who abase themselves.”*</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="6" style="v" sid="1PE 5:6"/>
    Therefore lower yourselves beneath the sovereign authority of God, that He may elevate you when the moment arrives.
    <verse eid="1PE 5:6"/>
  </para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="7" style="v" sid="1PE 5:7"/>
    Transfer the entirety of your burdens onto Him, for you occupy His concern.
    <verse eid="1PE 5:7"/>
  </para>
  <para style="s1">Firmness in the Faith</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="8" style="v" sid="1PE 5:8"/>
    Maintain vigilance and sobriety of mind. Your adversary, the devil, circles about as a predatory lion seeking prey to consume.
    <verse eid="1PE 5:8"/>
  </para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="9" style="v" sid="1PE 5:9"/>
    Oppose him through unwavering adherence to the faith, recognizing that the brotherhood of believers dispersed across the earth endures identical tribulations.
    <verse eid="1PE 5:9"/>
  </para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="10" style="v" sid="1PE 5:10"/>
    Once you have endured affliction for a season, the God who dispenses every grace—He who summoned you into His everlasting glory through union with Christ—will personally perfect, stabilize, fortify, and ground you.
    <verse eid="1PE 5:10"/>
  </para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="11" style="v" sid="1PE 5:11"/>
    To Him belongs dominion through all ages. Amen.
    <verse eid="1PE 5:11"/>
  </para>
  <para style="s1">Final Greetings</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="12" style="v" sid="1PE 5:12"/>
    By means of Silvanus, whom I consider a trustworthy brother in the faith, I have composed this concise correspondence to exhort you and to affirm that this is the authentic grace of God. Remain steadfast within it.
    <verse eid="1PE 5:12"/>
  </para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="13" style="v" sid="1PE 5:13"/>
    She who is in Babylon, elected alongside you, extends salutations, as does Mark, whom I regard as my spiritual son.
    <verse eid="1PE 5:13"/>
  </para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="14" style="v" sid="1PE 5:14"/>
    Exchange greetings with one another through the kiss of love. Peace to all who dwell in Christ.
    <verse eid="1PE 5:14"/>
  </para>
  <para style="s1">Notes</para>
  <para style="p">5 Quoted from Prov. 3:34</para>
  <chapter eid="1PE 5"/>
</usx>
